  "body": "@tabatkins tried to link to the definition of \"the head element\" [here](https://www.w3.org/TR/css-color-adjust-1/#color-scheme-meta) but since it's not exported, the link isn't generating. If it's a concept that needs to be used outside the HTML spec, maybe it should be.\r\n\r\nWhile we're on the topic, though, could it use a little more specific terminology? We have the \"document element\" for the root HTML, maybe the \"document head element\" for this term would be more clearly distinct from generic uses of \"head element\" (likewise for title/body)? It would also avoid having 'the-head-element-2' as the associated incoming target... it's nice to avoid auto-generated counters in IDs, they're less likely to accidentally change that way.",
